    android:viewportHeight="700">

    <!--
        THE MASK IS A CIRCLE 2/3 THE WIDTH OF THIS DRAWABLE, AND EVERYTHING
        OUTSIDE IT IS INVISIBLE.

        Android's splash icon is specified like an adaptive icon: the system
        crops the icon to a centred circle whose diameter is two thirds of the
        icon area (developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/launch/splash-screen).
        Before this group existed, the artwork's ink reached 321 units from the
        centre of a 700 viewport — the visible circle's radius is 233 — so 51.5%
        of the sampled outline lived outside the mask. That is the "circle cuts
        part of the logo" report: the tips of the M were simply not drawn.

        `logo_fit` scales the whole thing by 0.68 about the artwork's own centre
        (see the bbox below), which puts the furthest ink at 0.68 x 321 = 218
        units — inside 233 with the intro's own settle, which only ever scales
        UP from 0.94 to 1 and then stops. (There is no idle scale any more; the
        mask check reads every scale animator's peak from `Logo/miori_*.xml`
        rather than trusting a constant here.) It is a static group; the
        animated one stays `logo_group`, so the AVD targets and the choreography
        do not move.

        The alternative was to enlarge `imageWidth`: it scales the mask with the
        icon, so the clipping ratio would not change at all. Only the artwork
        can fix this.
    -->
    <group
        android:name="logo_fit"
        android:pivotX="350"
        android:pivotY="350"
        android:scaleX="0.68"
        android:scaleY="0.68">

    <!--
        PIVOT = 350,350 = THE ARTWORK'S OWN CENTRE (bbox centre 349.8, 350.6).
        The zoom therefore grows from the logo, not from the canvas, and the
        fit group above keeps it centred inside the mask.

        SCALE STARTS AT 1 — the FINISHED value. See the note on the paths below
        about why the static state is the logo, not a frame of the animation.
    -->
    <group
        android:name="logo_group"
        android:pivotX="350"
        android:pivotY="350"
        android:scaleX="1"
        android:scaleY="1">

